ffi: failed dlopen() leaks the libuv error message

### Version

main

### Platform

```text
macOS
```

### Subsystem

ffi

### What steps will reproduce the bug?

```js
import { dlopen } from 'node:ffi';

const path = '/nonexistent/' + 'x'.repeat(200) + '.dylib';
const run = (n) => {
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    try { dlopen(path, {}); } catch {}
  }
};

run(1000);
globalThis.gc();
const before = process.memoryUsage().rss;

run(400000);
globalThis.gc();
console.log((process.memoryUsage().rss - before) / 400000, 'B/call');
```

Run with
```console
node --no-warnings --expose-gc repro.mjs
```

### How often does it reproduce? Is there a required condition?

Always

### What is the expected behavior? Why is that the expected behavior?

A failed `dlopen()` should not hold on to native memory. RSS stays flat
```console
14.45888 B/call
```

### What do you see instead?

```console
1042.55488 B/call
```

RSS goes up by about 1 KB for each failed call (60 -> 477 MB over 400k calls).

