New Rule: `prefer-temporal`

### Rule details

Report creating or parsing dates with the global `Date` (`new Date()`, `Date()`, `Date.parse()`, `Date.UTC()`) and point to the matching `Temporal` API.

### Related ECMAScript feature

[Temporal](https://github.com/tc39/proposal-temporal)

### What type of rule is this?

Suggests an alternate way of doing something

### Example code

```js
/* eslint prefer-temporal: "error" */

// Reported
new Date();
new Date(1767225600000);
new Date("2026-01-15");
new Date(2026, 0, 15);
Date();
Date.parse("2026-01-15T10:00:00Z");
Date.UTC(2026, 0, 15);
```

### Why should this rule be in the core instead of a plugin?

Temporal is the built-in replacement for `Date`, so this fits the policy for rules about new ECMAScript features, like `prefer-object-has-own` did for `Object.hasOwn`.

